# house-pause-save — open the PAUSE menu (ESC), navigate to SAVE (entry type 3),
# and press Z (A=0x10) to open the type-3 save submenu.  Derived from house-pause
# (load fa7c82 → HOUSE free-roam idle, {phasepin 80}+{rngseed [80,19937]}).
#
# Nav: the house pause list is [1,6,2,3,4] = Items·Encyclopedia·Options·Save·Exit,
# default selection index 0 (Items).  Save is index 3 ⇒ THREE downs (the
# user-recalled "2x down" was off by one; verified via the v3 state panel).
#   sel 0 Items → (down) 1 Encyclopedia → (down) 2 Options → (down) 3 Save → (A) open.
#
# Sync: the pause-menu asset load (FUN_00473a3e, 20 sprites) stretches a DIFFERENT
# frame count per side (port ~1f, retail ~1800f) AND retail's pause never sets the
# b150 cursor flag PAUSE_OPEN keys on (so PAUSE_OPEN fires only on the port, and
# pre-load).  So the nav + caprange rebase on PAUSE_READY — the pause-load-done
# edge gated on scene mode 9, which fires once post-load on BOTH sides (the menu is
# navigable) — with a +30 margin for the open-slide (ramp 3→0xc) to settle.
# PAUSE_READY-relative nav is then identical on both sides → the v3 identity-join
# pairs the submenu frames cleanly past the (per-side-variable) load seam.
